# __PROJECT__

A PostgreSQL extension written in C# and published with .NET Native AOT.

Requires .NET 10, a native C toolchain, and PostgreSQL 18 or later with server headers.
Register PostgreSQL once:

```sh
ankus init --pg18 /path/to/pg_config
```

From this directory:

```sh
dotnet test
ankus publish
```

The tests check ordinary C# calls and publish the extension into an isolated
PostgreSQL cluster. Missing prerequisites fail the test run. Server logs remain
under `src/__PROJECT__/bin/ankus-test-logs/`; the cluster and temporary published
files are removed when the fixture is disposed.

Install and call the extension:

```sh
ankus install
```

```sql
CREATE EXTENSION __EXTENSION__;
SELECT add(40, 2), greet('PostgreSQL');
```

Add attributed functions in `src/__PROJECT__/Functions.cs`. Ankus generates the
native wrappers and SQL. Set `AnkusExtensionVersion` in the extension project
before publishing a new extension version. Package versions live in `global.json`
and `Directory.Packages.props`.
